plugin-db-qualification (2026110901) unstable; urgency=medium

  * One package, plugin-qualification-records, the same name on every
    platform, built per architecture. Its files stay at
    /usr/share/omx/qualification/<host class>/<set>/ and plugin-qualify-sync
    chooses the set of the machine's class and cell.
  * arm64: the rpi5 class, the zynthian-vangelis set, hardware tier
    (measured on the machine's own audio interface: the verdicts hold, the
    figures describe that interface). Depends on plugin-qualify >= 0.20.0
    and < 0.21. Released first, as a Debian package for trixie and
    bookworm.
  * amd64 and x86_64: the x86-64 class, ten fedora44 sets, one per cell, of
    1109 records of 668 plugins, at 48000/64, 48000/128, 48000/256,
    48000/512, 96000/64, 96000/128, 96000/256, 96000/512, 192000/256 and
    192000/512, provisional tier: measured by plugin-qualify-sync on JACK's
    dummy driver without real-time priority, host profile omx-clap-host.
    The crash, hang and unmeasured verdicts hold; the cost, latency and
    xrun figures are not reference figures. Eight sets ran plugin-qualify
    0.19.1, plugin-hostd 0.19.1 and omx-clap-host 0.30.6; 48000/128 and
    48000/256 ran 0.20.0, 0.20.0 and 0.31.0. Each set's provenance names
    its packages. 192000/128 is not here: its run did not finish. Depends
    on plugin-qualify >= 0.20.1 and < 0.21, which takes a set by its cell.
    Released in a later version, once that plugin-qualify is in the
    channel. There is no aarch64 RPM: no Fedora machine of an arm64 class
    is measured.
  * The older names are folded into it. The Debian package Provides,
    Replaces and Breaks plugin-db-qualification-rpi5-zynthian-vangelis and
    omx-qualification-rpi5-zynthian-vangelis on every architecture, and on
    amd64 also the x86-64 names: plugin-db-qualification-x86-64-fedora44,
    omx-qualification-x86-64-fedora44 and every per-cell
    plugin-db-qualification-x86-64-fedora44-<rate>-<quantum>. The x86_64
    RPM Provides and Obsoletes the x86-64 names. The list is derived from
    records/ when the package is built.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Mon, 09 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0100

plugin-db-qualification (2026110602) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The rpi5 zynthian-vangelis set measured again by plugin-qualify 0.19:
    1863 records, every LV2 plugin also run under omx-clap-host's LV2
    adapter on a private JACK server (0 adapter runs owed), then the
    isolated, pool and memory steps and a rejudge. Six bundles whose
    directory name holds a space are not in the set: the sync cannot read
    their files yet.
  * Renamed from omx-qualification-records: the repository and the packages
    are the qualification layer of plugin-db, plugin-db-qualification and
    plugin-db-qualification-<host class>-<set>. The install path stays
    /usr/share/omx/qualification/<host class>/<set>/.
  * One current set per machine class, measured by the latest plugin-qualify:
    the Fedora 44 x86-64 set (plugin-qualify 0.18.5) is dropped and ships
    again when it is measured with 0.19.
  * Depends on plugin-qualify >= 0.19.0 and < 0.20.

 -- Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>  Fri, 06 Nov 2026 18:00:00 +0100

